### LeetCode Username

pranaysah7

### Problem Number, Title, and Link

https://leetcode.com/problems/find-a-peak-element-ii/

### Bug Category

Missing test case *(Incorrect/Inefficient Code getting accepted because of missing test cases)*

### Bug Description

[[1,2,3],[8,16,4],[7,6,5]]
My code is only checking for corners but for the above test is failing.

### Language Used for Code

C++

### Code used for Submit/Run operation

```bash
class Solution {
public:
    vector<int> findPeakGrid(vector<vector<int>>& mat) {
        int n=mat.size(),m=mat[0].size();
        int dx[]={1,-1,0,0};
        int dy[]={0,0,-1,1};
        auto check=[&](int i,int j){

            int maxo=mat[i][j];
            for(int k=0;k<4;k++){
                int nx=i+dx[k];
                int ny=j+dy[k];
                if(nx>=0 and ny>=0 and nx<n and ny<m){
                    maxo=max(maxo,mat[nx][ny]);
                }
            }
            return maxo==mat[i][j];
        };
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
            if(check(i,0)){
                return {i,0};
            }
            if(check(i,m-1))
            return {i,m-1};
        }
        for(int i=0;i<m;i++){
            if(check(0,i)){
                return {0,i};
            }
            if(check(n-1,i))
            return {n-1,i};
        }
        return {0,0};
    }
};
```


### Expected behavior

expected failed but passed all test.

